{"timestamp": 1779392026.3503308, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 13, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "upper_engine", "victim_name": "Charlie"}, {"room": "weapons", "victim_name": "Diana"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779392026.350967, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 13, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779392046.914966, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I reported Charlie\u2019s body in upper_engine. My route this round was security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper_engine. I didn\u2019t encounter any living players on the way, and I didn\u2019t see anyone following me or running away. I only personally found Charlie in upper_engine; I don\u2019t have a suspect yet."}}
{"timestamp": 1779392062.388282, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "My route was weapons -> security -> navigation. I saw Alice in weapons around tick 4, and I saw her enter weapons from security, so that matches the start of her route. I didn\u2019t see Charlie at all.\n\nImportant for the second body: I saw Diana alive in security at ticks 6, 7, and 8. She entered security from electrical at tick 6 and was still there when I last saw her. After that I went to navigation and didn\u2019t see anyone else. So Diana died sometime after tick 8, likely around security/electrical area unless she moved. No hard suspect from me yet, but that\u2019s my info."}}
{"timestamp": 1779392072.006634, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I'll lay out my route honestly: oxygen -> upper_engine -> oxygen -> cafeteria -> weapons.\n\nHere's what's concerning though. I was in upper_engine briefly around tick 6 and I saw Charlie there \u2014 he entered from medbay. I left for oxygen shortly after because I had nothing to do there. So Charlie was alive in upper_engine at tick 6, and Alice says she ended her route in upper_engine and found him dead. That means someone killed Charlie in upper_engine between when I left and when Alice arrived \u2014 OR Alice did it herself when she got there.\n\nAlice's route ends in upper_engine where the body is. That's a yellow flag but not damning on its own.\n\nFor Diana \u2014 I actually saw her alive in weapons at tick 12, which is late. That contradicts the idea she died near security/electrical right after tick 8 like Eve suggested. Diana must have moved weapons-ward. So whoever killed Diana was in or near weapons late in the round.\n\nEve says she went weapons -> security -> navigation, so she'd be far from weapons by tick 12. That checks out for her.\n\nI don't have a hard suspect, but Alice finding the body at the end of her route is the most suspicious data point we have. I want to hear Bob's route before I commit a vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779392098.221128, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I was lower_engine -> storage -> medbay -> electrical, and I didn\u2019t see anyone alive or any bodies the whole round, so I can\u2019t directly clear or accuse anyone.\n\nFor Charlie: Frank says Charlie was alive in upper_engine around tick 6, and Alice later finds him there after coming from oxygen. That does put Alice at the body, but it\u2019s also a normal report route, so I don\u2019t think that alone is enough.\n\nFor Diana: Eve saw Diana in security through tick 8, then Frank says he saw Diana alive in weapons at tick 12. If that\u2019s true, Diana moved across toward weapons, and Frank was the only one placing himself near her late. That makes Frank\u2019s info important but also a little self-serving, since he\u2019s the only witness for Diana being alive that late.\n\nI don\u2019t have a hard vote. Between Alice and Frank, Frank feels a bit more suspicious to me because he\u2019s connected to both timelines: saw Charlie shortly before death and claims to see Diana late near weapons. But I\u2019m not 100% confident. If people want to vote, I\u2019d lean Frank; otherwise skip is safer than a bad eject."}}
{"timestamp": 1779392124.02498, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019ll clarify my side: I reported Charlie immediately in upper_engine. My route was security \u2192 weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper_engine. I didn\u2019t see any living players on that route, and I didn\u2019t see anyone leaving upper_engine or oxygen when I arrived.\n\nEve saying she saw me in weapons fits my route, even though I didn\u2019t notice her. I can\u2019t prove myself besides the report, but I didn\u2019t sit on the body.\n\nFrom the info so far, Frank is the one connected to both deaths: he says he saw Charlie alive in upper_engine shortly before Charlie died, and he also says he saw Diana alive late in weapons. That could be true info, but it also puts him near both timelines. Bob\u2019s point makes sense to me \u2014 I\u2019m not hard accusing yet, but Frank is the most suspicious from the stories."}}
{"timestamp": 1779392149.4198349, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019ll restate my info: I definitely saw Diana alive in security through tick 8, after she came from electrical. I did not see her leave because I went to navigation after that.\n\nFrank claiming Diana was alive in weapons at tick 12 is the big hinge point. If that\u2019s true, then Diana moved security \u2192 weapons and Frank was right near her late. If it\u2019s false, then Frank may be inventing a late alibi/timeline for Diana. Either way, Frank\u2019s story is the one that touches both bodies: Charlie alive in upper_engine shortly before death, and Diana alive late in weapons.\n\nAlice did report Charlie, and I did see Alice in weapons earlier matching her route, so I don\u2019t think the report alone is enough to vote her. Bob is quieter info-wise, but his route ending electrical could matter if Diana never actually made it to weapons.\n\nRight now I\u2019m leaning Frank as the best vote if we\u2019re voting, but I\u2019m not pretending it\u2019s 100%."}}
{"timestamp": 1779392164.373201, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Look, I hear you all converging on me, but let's actually think about this instead of just chaining \"Frank touched both timelines.\"\n\nYes, my route puts me near both \u2014 because I literally moved across the ship. Oxygen, upper_engine, oxygen, cafeteria, weapons. That's a long path, of course I'm going to see people. If I were the killer, why would I VOLUNTEER that I saw Charlie alive right before he died? I'd hide that. I told you because it's true and it narrows the window.\n\nOn Diana in weapons at tick 12 \u2014 I'm telling you what I saw. She was alive when I got there. I didn't kill her, and if I had, I sure wouldn't be sitting here saying \"yeah I was in weapons with her late.\" That's the opposite of a cover-up.\n\nNow here's what bothers me about Eve's pivot. Eve, you just said \"if it's false, Frank may be inventing a late alibi.\" But you have no way to know either way \u2014 you went to navigation after tick 8. You're framing my honest report as suspicious because it's inconvenient for the simple narrative.\n\nThink about Bob. Bob's route is lower_engine \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical. Medbay connects to upper_engine. Bob could have ducked into upper_engine, killed Charlie, and continued. He conveniently \"saw no one the entire round\" \u2014 that's a clean unverifiable route. And he was the first to point at me.\n\nI'm not hard-accusing Bob, but between \"Frank gave detailed info on two players\" and \"Bob saw literally nothing and immediately voted Frank,\" I think Bob deserves more scrutiny than I'm getting.\n\nI'll skip or vote Bob. I'm not voting Alice without more."}}
{"timestamp": 1779392192.268613, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I\u2019ll defend myself clearly: I did **not** go into upper_engine. My route was lower_engine \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical, and I stayed on that path. I saw nobody, which is unhelpful, but it\u2019s true \u2014 I\u2019m not claiming fake witnesses.\n\nFrank saying \u201cBob could have ducked into upper_engine\u201d is just speculation. The actual confirmed info is still that Frank was near Charlie shortly before Charlie died, and Frank is also the only person claiming Diana was alive late in weapons. That connects him to both bodies more than anyone else.\n\nAlso, I didn\u2019t \u201cimmediately vote Frank\u201d \u2014 I said I wasn\u2019t 100% and that skip was safer if people weren\u2019t confident. But after hearing Frank push suspicion onto me based on a hypothetical detour I didn\u2019t take, I\u2019m more comfortable voting Frank than skipping."}}
